{"duration_api_ms":6172,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d46c814a-cacf-4f81-9c27-f5269d84f909","total_cost_usd":0.0007473,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":668,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":963,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":614},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":668,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":963,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":668,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":668},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1212,"outputTokens":985,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":668,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0007473,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":614,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":668,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**No.** An Irish ICAV (Irish Collective Asset-management Vehicle, under the ICAV Act 2015) is a single body corporate with its own legal personality. Its sub-funds are compartments of that entity, not separate legal persons. They cannot sue, be sued, or contract in their own names. The ICAV does so on their behalf.\n\n**Segregated liability** is therefore statutory rather than inherent. The Act provides that assets attributable to one sub-fund are not available to meet liabilities of another. Creditors of a sub-fund generally have recourse only to that sub-fund's assets. Practice is to name the relevant sub-fund in contracts and to keep separate books and records.\n\n**The limitation** is that segregation depends on the ICAV's statutory framework. Its protection is only as strong as a foreign court's willingness to recognise it, which is weaker than true separate personality. Cross-border counterparties and insolvency practitioners in some jurisdictions may test it. Investors and counterparties often mitigate this with contractual provisions and legal opinions.","ttft_ms":3892,"type":"result","duration_ms":5643,"uuid":"59cd41da-1331-437a-a651-b31c383247c6","ttft_stream_ms":883,"time_to_request_ms":94,"first_content_frame_ms":883,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
